{"repositoryId":1182334724,"availability":"available","full":"loft-lang/loft","name":"loft","description":"A statically-typed scripting language inspired by Rust","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":8,"forks":1,"created":"2026-03-15T11:31:22Z","updated":"2026-10-19T21:59:25Z","license":"LGPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://loft-lang.org/loft/","topics":["compiler","game-development","interpreter","programming-language","rust","small-language","statically-typed","webassembly","webgl"],"demo":"https://loft-lang.org/loft/playground.html","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T22:20:13.042Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T22:20:13.042Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T22:20:13.042Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-19T22:20:13.042Z","stars":8,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["▶ Try it in the browser · 📘 Docs · 🎮 Play Brick Buster · 🖼 Gallery · ✍ Blog","loft is a statically typed language with almost no type annotations. The same source compiles to a native binary through rustc, to WebAssembly for the browser, or runs on a tree-walking interpreter for instant startup. It ships as a distribution: the compiler, a standard library, and 42 libraries in a registry — graphics and 3D, an HTTP server and client, cryptography, text engines, geometry — each one itself written in loft, so they read, debug and ship like your own code.","vector, sorted, index and hash collections; bounded generics and interfaces; par(...) for parallel loops; yield for generators; match for pattern matching; ?? default for null safety; format strings like Rust's. Types are inferred, and mistakes are caught at compile time."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/loft-lang/loft/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"7ff160236ed3b487b33cf0ff631f255dc6cde17fa0c0b236f1b5db03a0a1febd","extractedAt":"2026-10-19T22:20:13.147Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T22:20:13.147Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"wha